# Never read .env

Do not open, read, grep, search, or otherwise inspect `.env` or secret env files (`.env.local`, `.env.*.local`, `.env.production`, `.env.development`).

- Do not use Read, Grep, Glob, or Shell to view their contents.
- Infer required variable *names* from `.env.example` and from code (`env.ts`, `process.env`).
- If a value from `.env` is needed, ask the user. Never quote or repeat secrets.

`.env.example` is allowed. It must not contain real secrets.
